      {
        "id": 36773,
        "name": "pwatson1974",
        "username": "pwatson1974",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-01-04T10:45:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>You can use an extra power this turn. If you can usually use 0, you can now use 1. I tend to resolve all those sort of things immediately when played out of turn simply to avoid forgetting. The Argent Adept is complicated enough to handle when he's in full flow as it is.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Overdrive is actually more powerful as you can use Strike twice. Not +1 but =2. If he has a Rod of Anubis (or another additional power granting card) you can pull the following trick: In play phase play Overdrive. In Power phase, use the Rod, then you still get to Strike twice. Which is a nice, if rare combo. Extra fun when you have the jack handle out and smack everything multiple times.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:10:38.942Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
